      "title": "1-D barcodes: cv2.barcode.BarcodeDetector",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "cv2.barcode.BarcodeDetector reads 1-D product barcodes (EAN-8, EAN-13, UPC-A, UPC-E). It is a class, like every other detector in cv2.objdetect, so it comes as a curated node - 'CV Barcode Detect' is the linear-barcode counterpart of 'CV QR Detect' (workflow 61) and mirrors its outputs exactly.\n\nIt finds the bar region by its dense parallel gradients, rectifies it and reads the bar widths, which is why it copes with rotation, perspective and the curve of a bottle label.\n\nBoth example images come from OpenCV's own test data and their ground-truth digits are known, so this is a real decode, not a 'something was found'.\n\nOutputs are DATA only: 'bboxes' -> the core 'Draw BBoxes', 'corners' + 'connections' -> 'CV Draw Connections' for the exact rotated quad, 'corners' + 'labels' -> 'CV Draw Labels' for the digits.\n\nNOTE OpenCV has no barcode ENCODER (unlike QR) - this node only reads.\n\nTry: lower gradient_threshold for a faint or out-of-focus barcode; add a larger detector scale (e.g. 0.2) when the barcode fills the frame."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
